        9,
        10
      ],
      "visual_content": {
        "content_type": "paragraph",
        "verbatim_text": "## 2. CLASSIFICATION OF REAL NUMBERS",
        "has_inline_latex": false
      },
      "display_directives": {
        "text_layer": "show",
        "visual_layer": "hide",
        "avatar_layer": "show",
        "flip_timing_sec": null
      }
    },
    {
      "segment_id": 4,
      "source_block_ids": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "visual_content": {
        "content_type": "paragraph",
        "bullet_points": [
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Definition:** Positive integers used for counting: 1, 2, 3, ..."
          },
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Example:** 7 (number of days in a week)."
          },
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Exam Tip:** Do not include 0."
          }
        ],
        "verbatim_text": "### 2.1 Natural Numbers (N)",
        "has_inline_latex": false
      },
      "display_directives": {
        "text_layer": "hide",
        "visual_layer": "show",
        "avatar_layer": "gesture_only",
        "flip_timing_sec": null
      }
    },
    {
      "segment_id": 5,
      "source_block_ids": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "visual_content": {
        "content_type": "paragraph",
        "bullet_points": [
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Definition:** Natural numbers plus 0: 0, 1, 2, ..."
          },
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Example:** 0 (no apples left)."
          },
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Property:** All whole numbers are integers and hence real."
          }
        ],
        "verbatim_text": "### 2.2 Whole Numbers (W)",
        "has_inline_latex": false
      },
      "display_directives": {
        "text_layer": "hide",
        "visual_layer": "show",
        "avatar_layer": "gesture_only",
        "flip_timing_sec": null
      }
    },
    {
      "segment_id": 6,
      "source_block_ids": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "visual_content": {
        "content_type": "paragraph",
        "bullet_points": [
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Definition:** Numbers expressible as  $p/q$ , where  $p$  and  $q$  are integers and  $q \\neq 0$ ."
          },
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Decimal Nature:** Terminating or non-terminating repeating."
          },
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Important Property:** Rational numbers have eventually repeating decimal expansions."
          }
        ],
        "verbatim_text": "### 2.4 Rational Numbers (Q)",
        "has_inline_latex": false
      },
      "display_directives": {
        "text_layer": "hide",
        "visual_layer": "show",
        "avatar_layer": "gesture_only",
        "flip_timing_sec": null
      }
    },
    {
      "segment_id": 7,
      "source_block_ids": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "visual_content": {
        "content_type": "bullet_list",
        "bullet_points": [
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Definition:** Numbers expressible as  $p/q$ , where  $p$  and  $q$  are integers and  $q \\neq 0$ ."
          },
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Decimal Nature:** Terminating or non-terminating repeating."
          },
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Examples:**  $-2/5$ , 0.2,  $7/3$ ."
          },
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "**Important Property:** Rational numbers have eventually repeating decimal expansions."
          }
        ],
        "verbatim_source": "- **Definition:** Numbers expressible as  $p/q$ , where  $p$  and  $q$  are integers and  $q \\neq 0$ .\n- **Decimal Nature:** Terminating or non-terminating repeating.\n- **Examples:**  $-2/5$ , 0.2,  $7/3$ .\n- **Important Property:** Rational numbers have eventually repeating decimal expansions."
